--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY ARITHMETIC (reproduced exactly from the web source — cross-platform value parity, NOT "corrected")
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The web widget (and its shared sibling WeeklySummaryCardWidget.tsx — a codebase-wide convention) feeds
  WeeklyDigestData through this transform before the shared <Delta>/<WidgetComparisonCard>:

    distMi  = (distanceKm ?? 0) * UNITS.KM_TO_MI(0.621371)
    dist    = convertDistanceFromSI(distMi, unitPrefs.distance)  = distMi / {km 1000 · mi 1609.344 · ft 0.3048}
              → fmtNumber(_,1) + distanceUnit ; higherIsBetter
    drives  = drives ?? 0  → fmtInt ; higherIsBetter
    energy  = energyKwh ?? 0  → fmtNumber(_,1) + "kWh" ; higherIsBetter
    effWhMi = (efficiency ?? 0) * UNITS.MI_TO_KM(1.60934)
    eff     = unitPrefs.distance=='mi' ? effWhMi*1.609344 : effWhMi  → fmtNumber(_,0) + Wh/{mi|km} ; lower-is-better
    Delta(display=percent): signed=cur-prev; pct = prev!=0 ? |signed/|prev||*100 : nil;
                            text = fmtNumber(pct,1)+"%" else "—"; arrow = +→up / −→down / 0→flat;
                            tone = signed==0 muted; (higher&&+)||(lower&&−) ? emerald : rose
    metrics = [] when !data → web EmptyState "No weekly data yet" (data present, even all-zero, → card)

  NOTE: the km→mi / Wh·km→Wh·mi pre-scale makes the ABSOLUTE distance/efficiency display values small,
  but every per-metric PERCENT delta is ratio-preserving and therefore unchanged. Parity means native
  renders byte-for-byte the same strings the web renders for the same input — pinned by executed asserts:
    mi: distance "0.0 mi" +25.0%↑(good) · drives "12" +20.0%↑(good) · energy "45.6 kWh" 0.0%→(muted) ·
        efficiency "647 Wh/mi" "—"↑(rose, prev=0)
    km: distance "0.1 km" +25.0%↑ · efficiency "402 Wh/km"
        drives 1234 vs 1500 → "1,234" 17.7%↓(rose) ; nil fields → "0.0"/"—" ; non-finite → 0/"0.0".

